  "signature_visual": {
    "slide_number": 4,
    "concept": "The Intelligibility Ruler: a single horizontal STI scale (0 to 1.0) banded with the IEC 60268-16:2020 qualitative categories (Bad <0.30, Poor 0.30-0.45, Fair 0.45-0.60, Good 0.60-0.75, Excellent >0.75), with callout markers pinning NFPA 72's emergency-voice floor (STI >= 0.45 at >= 90% of locations per acoustically distinguishable space; average >= 0.50) and ACRP 175's pier-style departure-lounge recommendation (minimum STI 0.45 with 10 dB(A) signal-to-noise). A shaded annotation at the low end labels where the loud, reverberant, cross-broadcast terminal lands — making the draft's central inversion ('the loud terminal is the unintelligible one') legible in seconds.",
    "visual_type": "annotated_threshold_scale",
